{"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01CxMDebMae9wxFmzjqvcsYk","input":{"command":"git add -A && git status --short && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\n0.23.0: reads scope to the current branch, and a closed reader can say ENOTCONN\n\n**Reads default to scoped.** `readEvents` applied reachability only when the\ncaller asked, and `cledger export` never asked — so a consumer reading the\nledger got every branch's conversations, including work abandoned and never\nmerged. Storage has been per-commit all along and push has been branch-scoped\nsince 0.14.0; reads were the last place \"the ledger\" still meant everything\nthis machine ever captured.\n\n`ReadOptions.reachableFrom` now defaults to `HEAD`. The fix sits in\n`readEvents` rather than in `export` precisely because the consumers that\nmatter — intent-recall and anything else using the library — never go through\nthe CLI. `export` gains `--all` alongside `--rev`, matching `log`.\n\nThe opt-out is an explicit `null`, not \"unset\": `undefined` means the caller\ndid not say, and resolves to HEAD. The callers that genuinely want every local\nevent are few and now say so where they stand — `scan` and `review` (a secret\ndoes not stop being one because its branch is not checked out), `inspect` (an\nevent id is a global handle), `renormalize` (otherwise it strands preserved\nlines on every branch but the current one), and `show <id>` (you named one\nconversation, so reachability is not the question you asked).\n\nTwo transport tests had been conflating \"the note arrived\" with \"the anchor is\nreachable from here\" — they build repos with deliberately unrelated history,\nso the events genuinely are unreachable. They now assert both facts separately\nrather than one by accident.\n\n**`ENOTCONN` is also a closed reader.** Follow-up to 0.22.0's stdout guard,\nwhich matched `EPIPE` alone. On macOS Node does not always back stdio with a\npipe, and writing to a socket-backed stdout whose peer has closed reports\n`ENOTCONN` — so `cledger log --json | head -1` still exited 1, stack trace\ngone but failure intact. It only reproduced under enough concurrent load to\nchange how far the teardown had progressed, which is why 0.22.0's suite passed.\n`ECONNRESET` is matched too, for the half-closed case. Which errno arrives is\nan accident of what file descriptor Node handed us, never of what the user did.\n\nThe test now asserts stderr is *empty* rather than free of one named errno —\nthe narrower assertion passed while the command was still broken.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013a944mewfSjMmV598jZzFb\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"opencode-stable-seq","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"a67735deb89658e859eb93287ce9a1491ec9d37f","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-f02183fe3ee9e25d636fe3673dd0ce2a873df6fb7985feae715e7d1fc54b7890","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"224d1239-00ba-4ddb-8117-5a487d569b0d","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.235"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-19T02:17:13.944Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.25.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"reads-default-scoped","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01CxMDebMae9wxFmzjqvcsYk","input":{"command":"git add -A && git status --short && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\n0.23.0: reads scope to the current branch, and a closed reader can say ENOTCONN\n\n**Reads default to scoped.** `readEvents` applied reachability only when the\ncaller asked, and `cledger export` never asked — so a consumer reading the\nledger got every branch's conversations, including work