{"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01QdaNJuCyidxyRrrwEZuNd7","input":{"command":"git push -q -u origin codex-subagent-identity 2>&1|tail -3; gh pr create --base reads-default-scoped --title \"0.24.0: a codex sub-agent is its own conversation, not a corruption of its parent\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n> **Stacked on #7** (`reads-default-scoped`) — base it there so the diff shows only the codex commit. Rebases cleanly onto main once #7 lands.\n\nRoadmap item **\"Codex sub-agent coverage is unconfirmed.\"** It is now confirmed — and looking turned up a live bug, which is most of what this PR actually fixes.\n\n## Confirmed: codex writes one rollout per sub-agent thread\n\nMeasured on 40 local rollouts from Codex 0.146.0:\n\n| | count |\n|---|---|\n| top-level rollouts (`source` is a string: `cli` 22, `exec` 5, `vscode` 2) | 29 |\n| sub-agent rollouts (`source` is an object with a `subagent` key) | 11 |\n| of those, carrying `parent_thread_id` | 11 |\n\nThey sit in the same flat `YYYY/MM/DD/` tree with **no distinguishing filename**, and they hold real conversation — messages, reasoning, tool calls, plus 185 `sub_agent_activity` records of their own, so the nesting is recursive.\n\n## The bug this exposed\n\nThe adapter keyed a session on `session_meta.payload.session_id`. **On a child rollout, that field holds the parent's id.** Two silent consequences:\n\n1. A child's turns were filed into the **parent's** conversation, while numbered by the child's own line index — interleaving nonsense into the parent's `seq` ordering.\n2. The capture cursor, keyed on the same id, was **shared** between parent and child, each dragging the other into a full rescan.\n\nKeying on `payload.id` fixes both, and the no-churn property is measured rather than assumed:\n\n| field | equals the filename uuid |\n|---|---|\n| `payload.id` | **40 of 40** |\n| `payload.session_id` | 29 of 40 (exactly the top-level ones) |\n\nSo every top-level event id is unchanged, and only the children move — and they were mis-filed to begin with. A child now records `conversation.parent`, the same shape claude-code sidechains and opencode child sessions already use.\n\n**On where the parent link is applied:** in one exhaustive pass over the finished drafts, not threaded through the six places that construct one. The parent is a property of the *file* — identical for every event in it — and a single loop cannot miss a construction site the way six separate arguments could. It runs before the append, since `conversation.parent` is part of event identity.\n\n## Not shipped: discovery\n\n`event_msg/sub_agent_activity` carries an `agent_thread_id`, and 5 of the 6 distinct values seen resolve to a rollout file on disk (the sixth was presumably pruned) — so `agent_thread_id` → `rollout-*-<id>.jsonl` is a working trail, the codex analogue of claude-code's `subagents/` sibling directory.\n\ncledger does not walk it: capture only ever reads the transcript it was handed. So a codex sub-agent is captured **correctly if** something hands cledger its rollout, and whether codex fires a hook per child thread is **unverified** — no codex session has ever been captured in this repo to check against, so I could not settle it empirically. The roadmap now says correct-but-not-guaranteed rather than claiming parity with the other two adapters.\n\n## Testing\n\n`npm test`: **230 tests, 230 pass, 0 fail.**\n\nThree new codex tests, with shapes taken from the real rollouts above: a sub-agent rollout becomes its own conversation under its parent (and *every* event in the file carries the link, not just the turns); a top-level rollout keeps its id and gains no parent (the no-churn guarantee); and parent and child no longer share a capture cursor — the parent re-runs with `appended === 0` after the child is captured, which fails if the cursor is clobbered.\n\nConfirmed non-vacuous: restoring the old `session_id` preference makes the sub-agent test fail. The eight pre-existing codex tests pass unchanged, which is itself the evidence that top-level identity did not move.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_013a944mewfSjMmV598jZzFb\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -3"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"opencode-stable-seq","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"a67735deb89658e859eb93287ce9a1491ec9d37f","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-d9a1a2945de5a282f99ac870e8e67c75ce1b4511ac5cd7351a750d0088f67ac6","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"224d1239-00ba-4ddb-8117-5a487d569b0d","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.235"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-19T02:22:40.910Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.25.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"codex-subagent-identity","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01QdaNJuCyidxyRrrwEZuNd7","input":{"command":"git push -q -u origin codex-subagent-identity 2>&1|tail -3; gh pr create --base reads-default-scoped --title \"0.24.0: a codex sub-agent is its own conversation, not a corruption of its parent\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n> **Stacked on #7** (`reads-default-scoped`) — base it there so the diff shows only the codex commit. Rebases cleanly onto main once #7 lands.\n\nRoadmap item **\"Codex sub-agent coverage is unconfirmed.\"** It is now confirmed — and looking turned up a live bug, which is most of what this PR actually fixes.\n\n## Confirmed: codex writes one rollout per sub-agent thread\n\nMeasured on 40 local rollouts from Codex 0.146.0:\n\n| | count |\n|---|---|\n| top-level rollouts (`source` is a string: `cli` 22, `exec` 5, `vscode` 2) | 29 |\n| sub-agent rollouts (`source` is an object with a `subagent` key) | 