{"content":{"blocks":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01SXo9R8AaSBxEjbufGnmDw9","input":{"command":"git checkout -q -b codex-subagent-identity && git add -A && git status --short && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\n0.24.0: a codex sub-agent is its own conversation, not a corruption of its parent\n\nConfirms the open question — codex *does* write a separate rollout per\nsub-agent thread — and fixes the live bug that looking for them turned up.\n\nMeasured on 40 local rollouts from Codex 0.146.0: 11 are sub-agent threads,\nsitting in the same flat YYYY/MM/DD tree with no distinguishing filename. A\nchild is told apart by the shape of `session_meta.payload.source` — a plain\nstring for a top-level session (cli 22, exec 5, vscode 2), an object carrying\na `subagent` key for a child — and all 11 carry `parent_thread_id`. They hold\nreal conversation: messages, reasoning, tool calls, and 185 sub_agent_activity\nrecords of their own, so the nesting is recursive.\n\n**The bug.** The adapter keyed a session on `session_meta.payload.session_id`,\nand on a child rollout that field holds the *parent's* id. A child's turns were\ntherefore filed into the parent's conversation while numbered by the child's\nown line index, interleaving nonsense into the parent's `seq` ordering; and the\ncapture cursor, keyed on the same id, was shared between parent and child, each\ndragging the other into a full rescan.\n\nKeying on `payload.id` fixes both and costs nothing: `payload.id` equals the\nfilename's uuid for all 40 files, while `session_id` does so for only the 29\ntop-level ones. Every top-level event id is unchanged — no churn — and only the\nchildren move, which were mis-filed to begin with. A child now records\n`conversation.parent`, the same shape claude-code sidechains and opencode child\nsessions already use.\n\nThe parent link is applied in one exhaustive pass over the finished drafts\nrather than threaded through the six places that build one: the parent is a\nproperty of the file, identical for every event in it, and a single loop cannot\nmiss a construction site the way six arguments could. It runs before the\nappend, since `conversation.parent` is part of event identity.\n\n**Not shipped: discovery.** `event_msg/sub_agent_activity` carries an\n`agent_thread_id`, and 5 of the 6 distinct values seen resolve to a rollout on\ndisk, so that is a working trail — the codex analogue of claude-code's\n`subagents/` sibling directory. cledger does not walk it; capture only reads\nthe transcript it is handed. So a codex sub-agent is captured correctly *if*\nsomething hands cledger its rollout, and whether codex fires a hook per child\nthread is unverified — no codex session has ever been captured in this repo to\ncheck against. Recorded in the roadmap as correct-but-not-guaranteed rather\nthan claimed as parity.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013a944mewfSjMmV598jZzFb\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1"},"name":"Bash","type":"tool_use"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"opencode-stable-seq","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"a67735deb89658e859eb93287ce9a1491ec9d37f","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-540f0026469a3f19f00aceeb44d540af016633ec37953c7e58c4f2617f1568df","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"224d1239-00ba-4ddb-8117-5a487d569b0d","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.235"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-19T02:22:10.566Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.25.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"reads-default-scoped","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"caller":{"type":"direct"},"id":"toolu_01SXo9R8AaSBxEjbufGnmDw9","input":{"command":"git checkout -q -b codex-subagent-identity && git add -A 