{"content":{"blocks":[{"text":"Sanity checks: working tree clean, `npm test` on the committed state passes 222/223 (1 pre-existing skip), and the EPIPE fix verified end-to-end against a real 323KB ledger (`export | head -1` → exit 0, empty stderr; threw before).\n\n**PR #6:** https://github.com/evintunador/conversation-ledger/pull/6 — branch `fix-epipe-hook-detach-actor-display`, version bumped to 0.22.0.\n\nWhat shipped:\n\n1. **EPIPE guard.** `process.stdout` gets an `error` listener; EPIPE exits 0, anything else reports and exits 1. Installed CLI-wide, not just around the JSON printers — `log`'s human format and `conversations` broke the same way. The non-obvious half: `write()` reports EPIPE *asynchronously*, so a synchronous loop finishes (buffering the whole ledger) before the handler ever fires — the bulk printers now honour backpressure, which is what makes the exit prompt rather than merely quiet.\n\n2. **Hook redirect removed.** New Gemini/Qwen installs write no ` >/dev/null 2>&1`, and `cledger install` strips it from existing hooks in place — same contract the timeout repair set. I could not re-run the original headless `qwen -p` case (needs a live Qwen session), and said so in the roadmap rather than implying it was verified.\n\n3. **Display filter keyed on actor.** A machinery event with a `human` actor shows by default; `--with-state` unchanged.\n\nTwo things worth flagging, both judgment calls I made rather than checking in:\n\n- **The roadmap's premise for #3 was half wrong.** \"`activity` already carries a real actor\" — a survey found exactly one call site in the codebase passing `human`, so the display change alone would have surfaced qwen slash commands and nothing else. I corrected two attributions where the source genuinely states who acted (Gemini `$rewindTo` → human, keeping `snapshot_drop` as system; Qwen `at_command` → human).\n- **I deliberately did *not* fix claude-code's `queue-operation`,** which looked like the same bug. Across 40 of your local transcripts, `enqueue` splits 126 harness-generated to 43 human-typed — so a blanket \"enqueue → human\" would be wrong ~75% of the time, and the only discriminator is a content-shape heuristic. Getting it wrong files machine-authored text under your git identity, which is the same failure in the more damaging direction. The rule I applied: attribute where the source states it, leave `system` where it'd have to be guessed from content. Documented in the roadmap with the measured numbers — easy to overrule if you'd rather take the heuristic.\n\nAttribution changes are forward-only (`actor` is part of event identity), so re-capturing an old session mints new ids for those records rather than deduping — id churn in machinery records, no content loss, no backfill.\n\nresult: PR #6 opened on conversation-ledger fixing all three top-priority roadmap items (EPIPE crash, hook output redirect, actor-keyed display filter) — 223 tests pass, v0.22.0.","type":"text"}],"role":"assistant"},"context":{"branch":"opencode-stable-seq","cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","head":"a67735deb89658e859eb93287ce9a1491ec9d37f","repo":"git@github.com:evintunador/conversation-ledger.git"},"id":"ev2-075143f32f6a672cb74d970f469d11c89d4edfea881b0dd9c2e7bb566be44b82","kind":"conversation_turn","meta":{"actor":{"id":"claude-opus-5","type":"agent"},"model":"claude-opus-5","session_id":"224d1239-00ba-4ddb-8117-5a487d569b0d","source":"claude-code","source_version":"2.1.235"},"occurred_at":"2026-08-19T01:54:00.876Z","producer":{"tool":"cledger","version":"0.25.0"},"raw":{"data":{"cwd":"/Users/evintunador/repos/evintunador/conversation-ledger","effort":"high","entrypoint":"cli","gitBranch":"fix-epipe-hook-detach-actor-display","isSidechain":false,"message":{"content":[{"text":"Sanity checks: working tree clean, `npm test` on the committed state passes 222/223 (1 pre-existing skip), and the EPIPE fix verified end-to-end against a real 323KB ledger (`export | head -1`